{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LS6hh416hhmC4if7E9Kwqa","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Translation of `quic/quic.h`.\n2\t//!\n3\t//! `quic.h` is the kitchen-sink public header for the\n4\t//! quic-core library: it defines the protocol error codes, the\n5\t//! transport-parameter identifiers, the application-facing enums, the\n6\t//! opaque QUIC / connection / path types, the public structs that\n7\t//! cross the API boundary (`TransportParameters`, `PathQuality`,\n8\t//! `PerAckState`, `CongestionAlgorithm`, …)\n9\t//! and the dozens of free functions that make up the application API.\n10\t//!\n11\t//! Phase 4: all function bodies have been filled in.\n12\t//!\n13\t//! Pointer-shape and translation policy notes that apply throughout\n14\t//! this module:\n15\t//!\n16\t//! * `Quic`, `Connection`, `Path` are\n17\t//!   opaque types defined in `internal.h`.  Phase 1 declares\n18\t//!   them as empty structs here so the public API can refer to them;\n19\t//!   the real layout lands when the internal header is translated.\n20\t//! * `struct sockaddr*` parameters and fields map to\n21\t//!   [`core::net::SocketAddr`].  The C source uses tagged unions of\n22\t//!   `sockaddr_in` / `sockaddr_in6`, which `SocketAddr` models\n23\t//!   directly.  Output parameters of type `struct sockaddr_storage*`\n24\t//!   become a `SocketAddr` returned by value.\n25\t//! * Function-pointer typedefs become traits (one trait per typedef\n26\t//!   by default).  Trait grouping is used for the four-function\n27\t//!   `CongestionAlgorithm` vtable, where the C side\n28\t//!   always installs the four together.\n29\t//! * `void*` \"callback context\" arguments are folded into the trait\n30\t//!   implementor's state.  Per-stream / per-path application\n31\t//!   contexts that flow through the stack (e.g. `stream_ctx`,\n32\t//!   `app_stream_ctx`) become `Option<Box<dyn core::any::Any>>` —\n33\t//!   the application produces them, downcasts on retrieval.\n34\t//! * C `int` / `int64_t` return values that encode 0/-1 or 0/error\n35\t//!   status become `Result<T, Error>`.  `i32` / `i64` are kept where\n36\t//!   the C value is a real integer (e.g., wake delays in microseconds,\n37\t//!   interface index).\n38\t//! * Single-bit `unsigned int : 1` bitfields collapse to `bool`.\n39\t//! * `va_list` has no Rust counterpart; the `_v` log helpers are\n40\t//!   omitted in favour of one entry point that takes\n41\t//!   `core::fmt::Arguments<'_>`.\n42\t//! * `extern` global state (`congestion_control_algorithms`)\n43\t//!   becomes accessor functions that hand out a borrowed slice; the\n44\t//!   companion `_nb_` length variable disappears (the slice carries\n45\t//!   its length).\n46\t\n47\t// Many translated functions mirror C signatures with >7 parameters.\n48\t// Builder patterns or signature reshaping were not part of Phase 1.\n49\t#![allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)]\n50\t\n51\tpub mod arena;\n52\tpub mod bbr;\n53\tpub mod bbr1;\n54\tpub mod binlog;\n55\tpub mod bytestream;\n56\tpub mod c4;\n57\tpub mod cc_common;\n58\tpub mod config;\n59\tpub mod crypto;\n60\tpub mod errors;\n61\tpub mod frames;\n62\tpub mod hash;\n63\tpub mod header_protection;\n64\tpub mod internal;\n65\tpub mod lb;\n66\tpub mod logger;\n67\tpub mod packet_loop;\n68\tpub mod performance_log;\n69\tpub mod qlog;\n70\tpub mod siphash;\n71\tpub mod socks;\n72\tpub mod socks_socket2;\n73\tpub mod splay;\n74\tpub mod stream;\n75\tpub mod sys;\n76\t#[cfg(test)]\n77\tpub mod tests;\n78\tpub mod textlog;\n79\tpub mod tls;\n80\tpub mod tls_api;"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e717f4e2-96a7-4752-b6de-ede097ef17e8","uuid":"d86bce0b-60f5-41a8-afe3-55822da82da7","timestamp":"2026-05-07T05:38:45.187Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/lib.rs","content":"//! Translation of `quic/quic.h`.\n//!\n//! `quic.h` is the kitchen-sink public header for the\n//! quic-core library: it defines the protocol error codes, the\n//! transport-parameter identifiers, the application-facing enums, the\n//! opaque QUIC / connection / path types, the public structs that\n//! cross the API boundary (`TransportParameters`, `PathQuality`,\n//! `PerAckState`, `CongestionAlgorithm`, …)\n//! and the dozens of free functions that make up the application API.\n//!\n//! Phase 4: all function bodies have been filled in.\n//!\n//! Pointer-shape and translation policy notes that apply throughout\n//! this module:\n//!\n//! * `Quic`, `Connection`, `Path` are\n//!   opaque types defined in `internal.h`.  Phase 1 declares\n//!   them as empty structs here so the public API can refer to them;\n//!   the real layout lands when the internal header is translated.\n//! * `struct sockaddr*` parameters and fields map to\n//!   [`core::net::SocketAddr`].  The C source uses tagged unions of\n//!   `sockaddr_in` / `sockaddr_in6`, which `SocketAddr` models\n//!   directly.  Output parameters of type `struct sockaddr_storage*`\n//!   become a `SocketAddr` returned by value.\n//! * Function-pointer typedefs become traits (one trait per typedef\n//!   by default).  Trait grouping is used for the four-function\n//!   `CongestionAlgorithm` vtable, where the C side\n//!   always installs the four together.\n//! * `void*` \"callback context\" arguments are folded into the trait\n//!   implementor's state.  Per-stream / per-path application\n//!   contexts that flow through the stack (e.g. `stream_ctx`,\n//!   `app_stream_ctx`) become `Option<Box<dyn core::any::Any>>` —\n//!   the application produces them, downcasts on retrieval.\n//! * C `int` / `int64_t` return values that encode 0/-1 or 0/error\n//!   status become `Result<T, Error>`.  `i32` / `i64` are kept where\n//!   the C value is a real integer (e.g., wake delays in microseconds,\n//!   interface index).\n//! * Single-bit `unsigned int : 1` bitfields collapse to `bool`.\n//! * `va_list` has no Rust counterpart; the `_v` log helpers are