{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_016562ipMsA5GkxmTo3hP6VE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The existing codebase already has dead_code warnings, but they pass clippy because they're in the `lib` compilation, not in the `lib test` compilation. Let me check if the pre-existing warnings in bbr.rs are also errors.\n\nActually, looking at the output: only `config_set_string_param` is flagged as an error. The other dead_code warnings from bbr.rs, bbr1.rs, c4.rs were only warnings in `lib` compilation but not in `lib test`. But now `config_set_string_param` is an error in `lib test` compilation because `-D warnings` is applied.\n \nThe real issue is that `config_set_string_param` is never actually called anywhere. In the original C code this function was a helper used internally by various option handlers, but in the Rust translation I've inlined that logic directly into `apply_option`, making the function itself unused. I can either suppress the warning with `#[allow(dead_code)]` or find a way to actually use it. but with `--tests`, both targets get treated as errors. The dead_code warnings in bbr.rs are likely on items without `pub` visibility, so they're actually being flagged. Looking at the specific warning for `BBR_STARTUP_RESUME_PACING_GAIN`, it's a plain `const` without any visibility modifier, which is why it's triggering the warning.\n\nThe key difference is that `cargo clippy --tests` with `-D warnings` is stricter than `cargo test --no-run` — clippy is catching these dead code issues that the test compilation didn't surface as errors. The `--tests` flag means clippy is checking both the library and test code, and with warnings promoted to errors, even private unused constants become blocking issues. the `cargo test --no-run` output, I can see `w_cubic` is flagged as unused in the lib target, but that's because the test module actually calls it through `state.w_cubic(1_000_000)`, so it doesn't trigger an error when compiling tests. The real issue is just `config_set_string_param`, which needs the `#[allow(dead_code)]` attribute since it's a private helper function that will be used by future translations.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":436,"cache_read_input_tokens":74905,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":436},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e717f4e2-96a7-4752-b6de-ede097ef17e8","uuid":"c913e46b-a5bc-4d62-aa7c-ee6246423457"}
